Although the past couple of years left a bitter taste, I decided to take a leap of faith and get the F1 2016 game on pre-purchase offer and it was a good decision
I've only played 5 hours of the game and the impressions are so much better than 2014/2015 versions.
Here are the things I most enjoyed during this short amount of time:
The career mode is what makes it all fun, choose a low-end team and race your way to the top;
Personalize your driver by choosing name, looks, nationality and obviously an Ayrton Senna like helmet;
You can develop the car (R&D) along the practice seasons by completing some goals that will also help you to drive better;
Control your entire career through your laptop;
Beating your teammate is always rewarding;
Get the best out of your car at the start of the race by feeding the throttle and releasing the clutch at the exact moment;
Watch the pre-race and post-race actions.
There are some downsides also:
The AI keeps hammering your rear wing under braking, so annoying;
There is still lots of wheel spin making it too arcade;
After the rain, the track starts to dry slowly and naturally but then hits a turning point where it gets completely dry out of the blue and it is hard to define which strategy to follow.
The FFB could be improved, the loose center is still there when using a G27 for example.
Overall, it is a good game and in one weekend, I've already played it much more than the previous two versions.

Despite watching youtubers play this game less than a year ago, I still really enjoyed playing this short indie horror game.
This game is getting mixed reviews, I would recommend this game IF you like:
* Beautiful artwork;
* Atmospheric music;
* Disturbing and confusing imagery and plot lines;
* Getting murdered many times (Limbo-style!);
* Creepy surround headphone effects.
This game plays like a maze more than anything. There aren't really puzzles to solve or enemies to battle, although you have to outsmart a few enemies by being stealthy. So don't play Neverending Nightmares if you need fights or detective work to enjoy a game.

